message: "If you use this software, please cite it using these metadata."
type: software
title: "Machine-Checked Worst-Case Noise Bounds for RNS BGV and BFV: IND-CPA-D Security and What It Costs"
abstract: >-
  ProvenFHE makes worst-case noise bounds, the countermeasure the IND-CPA-D attack papers
  recommend, checkable for RNS BGV and BFV. It provides fhe_check, a checker whose CERTIFIED
  verdict has a machine-checked Lean 4 soundness theorem covering the RNS algorithms libraries
  run (hybrid key switching, modulus switching, BEHZ and HPS-family multiplication with their
  binary64 sums), and a proof that on the circuits it accepts IND-CPA-D reduces to IND-CPA, for
  BGV and BFV, with textbook decryption and public evaluation keys: in the fresh-only game for
  every evaluator within the budget, and in the game with evaluation on earlier results for local
  step-by-step interpreters. It
  also provides provenfhe_ref, a reference implementation proved to compute the definitions the
  theorems are about, and a measured cost of certified parameters on OpenFHE. Existing libraries
  (OpenFHE, Lattigo) are tested instances, compared with the models on recorded runs.
